  "anti_overread": [
    "it does not assert that every promoted extension is useful, that hidden promoted objects are lower-layer content, or novelty for the classical constructions themselves.",
    "The scope is intentionally narrow.",
    "abstracts the shared shape into a typed profile skeleton and proves a transfer theorem: a profile validated in one case is portable to another under matching audit hypotheses, but the transfer remains conditional on target-side validation, so it does not identify objects across domains.",
    "It records the problem, the candidates the layer is allowed to try, the kind of answer that would count, the defect by which a candidate is judged, the threshold for passing, and the surrounding nonclaim register.",
    "A Strict Audited Utility (SAU) certificate is the bundled six-field record of saturation, strictness, non-descent, audited descent, accepted lower answer, and nonclaim register.",
    "These operations preserve the accepted lower answer, the bridge and audit records, and the nonclaim register, so the compressed trace is audit-equivalent to the original trace.",
    "In other words, ValSAU( C) records that each witness field has passed the declared checks, every bridge is admissible, and the nonclaim register has been recorded.",
    "Finally, the exact-six role vector records the same idea at the inherited six-role level: a role is usable only when it is present, aligned, thresholded, visible or bridged, audited, and nonclaim-safe."
